---
// Below the story: the framework in short, and what the data is. The seven
// steps above carry the explanation; this is the recap. Static HTML.
import { formatNumber } from '../../lib/format';
import { datasets } from './data';
import { share } from './math';

const dataset = datasets[0];
if (!dataset) throw new Error('A/B Testing has no data');
const { mean, sd } = dataset.history;
---

<div class="explain">
  <section aria-labelledby="ab-summary">
    <h2 id="ab-summary">A/B testing in short</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Ask</strong> one question, and randomize only the people the
        change can reach.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Measure</strong> one metric tied to the goal, plus guardrails
        that must not get worse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sign</strong> the contract first: α, power and the MDE, and from
        them the users and the days, in whole weeks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Run</strong> an A/A test, then the full plan, without stopping
        early.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Check</strong> the split, outside events and novelty before
        trusting any p-value.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Read</strong> the interval against 0 and the MDE, not just the
        p-value.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Decide</strong>, and make sure the lift pays for itself.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ab-data">
    <h2 id="ab-data">About the data</h2>
    <p>
      StylePulse and its numbers are made up, but they behave like a real
      shop’s: on a usual day {share(dataset.buyRate, 0)} of searchers buy
      something, so most spend $0, and spend per searcher averages{' '}
      {`$${formatNumber(mean, 2)}`} with a standard deviation of{' '}
      {`$${formatNumber(sd, 2)}`}. Each test was simulated searcher by searcher;
      the page gets each day’s totals for each group, which is all the test
      needs. Each searcher-day counts on its own here; real analyses group a
      person’s days together.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .explain {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-12);
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: var(--fs-16);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-24);
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.4em;
  }
</style>
